Most smoke machine rental pages sell the machine. This one starts somewhere else, because the machine is the easy part.

A fog machine is not a decoration. It exists for one reason: **light travelling through clean air is invisible**. You only see the beam when there is something in the air for it to hit. Rent lighting without fog and you get lit surfaces. Add fog and you get the beams themselves, which is the look almost everyone actually had in mind.

That is why this page sits under our [stage lighting rental](/blog/stage-lighting-rental/) guide rather than beside the speakers.

Malaga Event Gear stocks **one Martin Magnum 650**, and we sell it as a 20 euro add on rather than as a package of its own. Below is exactly what it does, what it does not do, and the one question that decides whether it can run at your venue at all.

## The Real Machine We Stock

One unit, and we would rather name it than hide behind "professional fog effects":

| Spec | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Model | Martin Magnum 650 |
| Power | 600 W |
| Output | 160 m3 per minute |
| Units in stock | 1 |
| Price | 20 euros, as an add on |

One machine is genuinely enough for a dancefloor, a stage or a single presentation area. It is not enough to fill a large hall evenly, and we are not going to tell you otherwise. If you have seen a venue wrapped corner to corner in fog, that was several machines placed around the room, not one. The extra machines are not in our own inventory, but tell us the room and we will look for them with our suppliers, if they are available.

## How You Get It: An Add On, Not a Package

